From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Fri, 07 Aug 2026 16:22:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi-scripts: fix EHT320 operating width enum values

eht_oper_chwidth used 7, which is CONF_OPER_CHWIDTH_8640MHZ (60 GHz
DMG); 320 MHz is 9. The 6 GHz beacon path masked this because the
EHT Operation width is derived from op_class 137, but
hostapd_get_oper_chwidth() feeds the ucode switch_channel width
selection, which fell through to 20/40 MHz on any EHT320 CSA, and
acs_adjust_center_freq() rejected the value outright, so ACS never
set a 320 MHz center frequency. The shell variant already emits 9.

he_oper_chwidth used 3 (80+80 MHz) for the HE 160 MHz backward
compatibility values; 160 MHz is 2, matching the comment and the
segment 0 selection. Inherited verbatim from upstream OpenWrt
files-ucode; the shell variant is unaffected.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 src/usr/share/ucode/wifi/hostapd.uc |    4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/src/usr/share/ucode/wifi/hostapd.uc
+++ b/src/usr/share/ucode/wifi/hostapd.uc
@@ -282,14 +282,14 @@ function device_htmode_append(config) {
 					break;
 				}
 			config.op_class = 137;
-			config.eht_oper_chwidth = 7;
+			config.eht_oper_chwidth = 9;
 
 			/*
 			 * Set HE operation values for 160MHz backward compatibility
 			 * with WiFi 6E clients. Pick the 160MHz half that contains
 			 * the primary channel.
 			 */
-			config.he_oper_chwidth = 3;
+			config.he_oper_chwidth = 2;
 			if (config.channel < config.eht_oper_centr_freq_seg0_idx)
 				config.he_oper_centr_freq_seg0_idx = config.eht_oper_centr_freq_seg0_idx - 16;
 			else
